IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap3-s2022`

-- TESTS for section 2022 (snap3-s2022.l4). Every expected value is worked out from the text of section 2022 and written beside the assertion, BEFORE running.

§ `Tests -- s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary's power over claims`

-- arguments: the decision, the claim is an at-risk amount or a State share, the Secretary's determination that waiving would serve the purposes of the chapter
-- determining the amount of a claim: a power (a claim arising from an overissuance)
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary has the power to make the decision about the claim` `establish a claim for an overissuance` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Except in the case of an at-risk amount ... or ... a State share": no power
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary has the power to make the decision about the claim` `establish a claim for an overissuance` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- waiving: "the power to waive claims if the Secretary determines that to do so would serve the purposes of this chapter"
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary has the power to make the decision about the claim` `grant a waiver` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary has the power to make the decision about the claim` `grant a waiver` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary has the power to make the decision about the claim` `grant a waiver` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary has the power to make the decision about the claim` `grant a waiver` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a decision the section does not speak of
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary has the power to make the decision about the claim` `deny an application` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary has the power to make the decision about the claim` `certify a household as eligible` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- delegation: "Such powers with respect to claims against recipients may be delegated by the Secretary to State agencies"
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary may delegate the powers over the claim to State agencies` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary may delegate the powers over the claim to State agencies` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- reducing amounts due to the State agency: arguments are an unpaid claim assessed against the State agency, the State agency declined or exhausted its appeal rights
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary may reduce amounts otherwise due to the State agency under section 2025 to collect the claim` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary may reduce amounts otherwise due to the State agency under section 2025 to collect the claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(1) the Secretary may reduce amounts otherwise due to the State agency under section 2025 to collect the claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2022(a)(2) interest on claims established under the quality control system`

-- liable: arguments are claim established under 2025(c)(1), paid or agreed within 30 days of the bill, the State agency appeals under 2025(c)(7)
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the State agency is liable for interest on the unpaid portion of the claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the State agency is liable for interest on the unpaid portion of the claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the State agency is liable for interest on the unpaid portion of the claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the State agency is liable for interest on the unpaid portion of the claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the date from which interest accrues: arguments are claim established, paid within 30 days, appeals, the date the bill was received, the date of the decision on the appeal if any
-- no appeal: from the date the bill was received
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the date from which interest on the unpaid portion accrues` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2026)
-- paid in time: no unpaid portion, no date
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the date from which interest on the unpaid portion accrues` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- not a claim under 2025(c)(1): not covered
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the date from which interest on the unpaid portion accrues` FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- appealed, decision on 1 September 2026, which is before 1 March 2027 (one year after the bill): from the decision
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the date from which interest on the unpaid portion accrues` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 9 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2026)
-- appealed, decision on 1 June 2027, after 1 March 2027: from the date a year after the bill
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the date from which interest on the unpaid portion accrues` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 6 2027)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2027)
-- appealed, decision exactly on the first anniversary: the same date either way
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the date from which interest on the unpaid portion accrues` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 3 2027)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2027)
-- appealed, one day before the anniversary: from the decision
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the date from which interest on the unpaid portion accrues` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 28 2 2027)) EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2027)
-- appealed, one day after the anniversary: from the anniversary
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the date from which interest on the unpaid portion accrues` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 2 3 2027)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2027)
-- appealed, no decision yet: the date a year after the bill is the only date there is
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the date from which interest on the unpaid portion accrues` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2027)
-- a bill received 29 February 2028: a year later has no 29 February; the module's date arithmetic clamps to 28 February 2029 (assumed, NOTES.md fork F-2022-1)
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the date from which interest on the unpaid portion accrues` TRUE FALSE TRUE (Date 29 2 2028) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2029)
-- overturned claim: arguments are the State agency paid in whole or in part, the claim was overturned on appeal
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the amounts paid by the State agency must be promptly returned with interest` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the amounts paid by the State agency must be promptly returned with interest` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(2) the amounts paid by the State agency must be promptly returned with interest` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2022(a)(3) computation of interest and (a)(4) joint and several liability`

#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(3) the rate at which interest is computed` (JUST 0.045) EQUALS JUST 0.045
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(3) the rate at which interest is computed` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- the average of weekly rates 4, 5 and 6 is 5; of one rate 3.5 is 3.5; of none there is no average
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(3) the average of the weekly 90-day Treasury bill auction rates` (LIST 4, 5, 6) EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(3) the average of the weekly 90-day Treasury bill auction rates` (LIST 3.5) EQUALS JUST 3.5
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(3) the average of the weekly 90-day Treasury bill auction rates` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a)(4) arguments: the group is a household (s 2012(m) answer), the member is an adult
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(4) the member is jointly and severally liable for the value of the overissuance` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(4) the member is jointly and severally liable for the value of the overissuance` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(4) the member is jointly and severally liable for the value of the overissuance` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(a)(4) the member is jointly and severally liable for the value of the overissuance` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2022(b) collection of overissuances`

-- (b)(1) arguments: an overissuance was issued, what paragraph (2) says
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(1) the State agency must collect the overissuance` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(1) the State agency must collect the overissuance` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(1) the State agency must collect the overissuance` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(1) the State agency must collect the overissuance` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the four means all appear in the list
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(1) the State agency may collect the overissuance by the means` `s 2022(b)(1)(A) reducing the allotment of the household` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(1) the State agency may collect the overissuance by the means` `s 2022(b)(1)(B) withholding amounts from unemployment compensation from a member of the household under subsection (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(1) the State agency may collect the overissuance by the means` `s 2022(b)(1)(C) recovering from Federal pay or a Federal income tax refund under subsection (d)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(1) the State agency may collect the overissuance by the means` `s 2022(b)(1)(D) any other means` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (b)(2)
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(2) paragraph (1) does not apply` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b)(3) the largest reduction: arguments are a member found ineligible under 2015(b)(1), the State agency elects to reduce the allotment, the monthly allotment
-- the greater of 10 percent of the monthly allotment and $10. 10 percent of 200 = 20
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the greatest reduction of the monthly allotment` FALSE TRUE 200 EQUALS JUST 20
-- allotment 100: 10 percent is exactly 10, the same as $10
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the greatest reduction of the monthly allotment` FALSE TRUE 100 EQUALS JUST 10
-- allotment 99: 10 percent is 9.90, so the $10 is the greater
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the greatest reduction of the monthly allotment` FALSE TRUE 99 EQUALS JUST 10
-- allotment 101: 10 percent is 10.10, the greater
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the greatest reduction of the monthly allotment` FALSE TRUE 101 EQUALS JUST 10.1
-- a member was found ineligible under 2015(b)(1) (fraud route), or the State agency does not reduce the allotment: the paragraph does not speak
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the greatest reduction of the monthly allotment` TRUE TRUE 200 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the greatest reduction of the monthly allotment` FALSE FALSE 200 EQUALS NOTHING
-- may reduce by the amount: arguments add the proposed reduction
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the State agency may reduce the monthly allotment by the amount` FALSE TRUE 200 20 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the State agency may reduce the monthly allotment by the amount` FALSE TRUE 200 20.01 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the State agency may reduce the monthly allotment by the amount` FALSE TRUE 100 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the State agency may reduce the monthly allotment by the amount` FALSE TRUE 100 10.01 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the State agency may reduce the monthly allotment by the amount` FALSE TRUE 50 10 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the State agency may reduce the monthly allotment by the amount` FALSE TRUE 50 10.01 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the State agency may reduce the monthly allotment by the amount` TRUE TRUE 200 50 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(3) the State agency may reduce the monthly allotment by the amount` FALSE FALSE 200 20 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b)(4) arguments: notice, the household elected a means of payment, a time schedule established, each in accordance with the State agency's requirements
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(4) the State agency collected the overissuance in accordance with its requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(4) the State agency collected the overissuance in accordance with its requirements` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(4) the State agency collected the overissuance in accordance with its requirements` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(4) the State agency collected the overissuance in accordance with its requirements` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- s 2022(b)(5) overissuances caused by systemic State errors`

-- (A) arguments: the Secretary's determination of a major systemic error, the Secretary has prohibited collection from the household
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(A) the State agency may collect the overissuance from the household` (JUST TRUE) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(A) the State agency may collect the overissuance from the household` (JUST TRUE) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(A) the State agency may collect the overissuance from the household` NOTHING TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(A) the State agency may collect the overissuance from the household` (JUST FALSE) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (B)(i)
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(i) the State agency has provided the information requested` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(i) the State agency has provided the information requested` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (B)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(ii) the Secretary has made the final determination` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(ii) the Secretary has made the final determination` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(ii) the Secretary has made the final determination` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(ii) the Secretary has made the final determination` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (B)(iii) a claim against the State agency, owed to the Secretary, equal to the value of the overissuance caused by the systemic error
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(iii) the claim against the State agency` TRUE 500000 EQUALS JUST (Claim WITH `amount in dollars` IS 500000, `owed by` IS `the State agency`, `owed to` IS `the Secretary`)
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(iii) the claim against the State agency` FALSE 500000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (B)(iv)
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(iv) administrative and judicial review under section 2023 applies to the determination` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(iv) administrative and judicial review under section 2023 applies to the determination` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (B)(v) arguments: the determination is appealed, review is complete, a finding of liability, the amount of the claim, the amount subject to the finding
-- not appealed: the dollar amount specified in the claim
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(v) the dollar amount the State agency must remit to the Secretary` FALSE FALSE FALSE 1000 0 EQUALS JUST 1000
-- appealed, review complete, liability found: the amount subject to the finding
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(v) the dollar amount the State agency must remit to the Secretary` TRUE TRUE TRUE 1000 600 EQUALS JUST 600
-- appealed, review not complete: nothing yet to remit
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(v) the dollar amount the State agency must remit to the Secretary` TRUE FALSE TRUE 1000 600 EQUALS NOTHING
-- appealed, review complete, no finding of liability: the text does not say
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(v) the dollar amount the State agency must remit to the Secretary` TRUE TRUE FALSE 1000 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (B)(vi)
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vi)(I) the Secretary may reduce any amount due to the State agency by the amount due` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vi)(I) the Secretary may reduce any amount due to the State agency by the amount due` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vi)(II) interest in the amount owed accrues` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vi)(II) interest in the amount owed accrues` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (B)(vii) arguments: the liability amount under 2025(c)(1)(C), the amount of the claim
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vii) the liability amount after the reduction` 1000 400 EQUALS JUST 600
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vii) the liability amount after the reduction` 400 400 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(5)(B)(vii) the liability amount after the reduction` 400 401 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2022(c) intercept of unemployment benefits`

-- (c)(1) the uncollected overissuance is the part not recovered
#ASSERT `s 2022(c)(1) the uncollected overissuance` 500 200 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 2022(c)(1) the uncollected overissuance` 500 0 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `s 2022(c)(1) the uncollected overissuance` 500 500 EQUALS 0
-- recovered more than the overissuance: nothing is left uncollected
#ASSERT `s 2022(c)(1) the uncollected overissuance` 500 600 EQUALS 0
-- (c)(2)
#ASSERT `s 2022(c)(2) the State agency may determine on a periodic basis whether the individual owes an uncollected overissuance` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(c)(2) the State agency may determine on a periodic basis whether the individual owes an uncollected overissuance` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c)(3) arguments: the individual is one described in (2), an agreement to withhold exists, a copy of it was furnished to the unemployment compensation agency, a court's writ or similar process was obtained
-- (A): an agreement and a copy furnished
#ASSERT `s 2022(c)(3) the State agency may recover the uncollected overissuance` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (A) incomplete: an agreement but no copy furnished, and no writ
#ASSERT `s 2022(c)(3) the State agency may recover the uncollected overissuance` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (B) is "in the absence of an agreement": a writ obtained although an agreement exists does not bring (B) into play
#ASSERT `s 2022(c)(3) the State agency may recover the uncollected overissuance` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (B): no agreement, a writ obtained
#ASSERT `s 2022(c)(3) the State agency may recover the uncollected overissuance` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither route taken
#ASSERT `s 2022(c)(3) the State agency may recover the uncollected overissuance` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not an individual described in paragraph (2)
#ASSERT `s 2022(c)(3) the State agency may recover the uncollected overissuance` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 2022(d) recovery of overissuance of benefits`

-- arguments: the amount not yet recovered, the source, the recovery is as authorized by section 5514 of title 5 or 3720A of title 31
#ASSERT `s 2022(d) the uncollected overissuance may be recovered from the source` 100 `s 2022(d) Federal pay (including salaries and pensions)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(d) the uncollected overissuance may be recovered from the source` 100 `s 2022(d) a Federal income tax refund` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 2022(d) the uncollected overissuance may be recovered from the source` 100 `s 2022(d) Federal pay (including salaries and pensions)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(d) the uncollected overissuance may be recovered from the source` 100 `s 2022(d) any other source` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 2022(d) the uncollected overissuance may be recovered from the source` 0 `s 2022(d) a Federal income tax refund` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- every constructor declared in snap3-s2022.l4 is built once`

#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(1)(A) reducing the allotment of the household` EQUALS `s 2022(b)(1)(A) reducing the allotment of the household`
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(1)(B) withholding amounts from unemployment compensation from a member of the household under subsection (c)` EQUALS `s 2022(b)(1)(B) withholding amounts from unemployment compensation from a member of the household under subsection (c)`
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(1)(C) recovering from Federal pay or a Federal income tax refund under subsection (d)` EQUALS `s 2022(b)(1)(C) recovering from Federal pay or a Federal income tax refund under subsection (d)`
#ASSERT `s 2022(b)(1)(D) any other means` EQUALS `s 2022(b)(1)(D) any other means`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2022(b)(1)(A) reducing the allotment of the household` EQUALS `s 2022(b)(1)(D) any other means`)
#ASSERT `s 2022(d) Federal pay (including salaries and pensions)` EQUALS `s 2022(d) Federal pay (including salaries and pensions)`
#ASSERT `s 2022(d) a Federal income tax refund` EQUALS `s 2022(d) a Federal income tax refund`
#ASSERT `s 2022(d) any other source` EQUALS `s 2022(d) any other source`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 2022(d) a Federal income tax refund` EQUALS `s 2022(d) any other source`)
